-- plan_merged: both proposals at once, and then a decision.
--
-- The world starts as the union of its parents. Every course is the same course in both
-- (same origin), so it carries the facts of both: two hours, sometimes two lecturers.
-- Nothing fails here. What doesn't fit is settled by stating what is true.

from plan_morning, plan_spread

? course c and count c.meets_at > 1       -- where the two plans disagree
? analysis_2.taught_by

analysis_2            [ taught_by: cauchy | meets_at: mon_14 ]
group_theory          [ meets_at: tue_11 ]
galois_theory         [ meets_at: wed_11 ]
differential_geometry [ meets_at: tue_14 ]

-- The parents also define `overloaded` two ways. Until it is restated it produces nothing.
? person t is overloaded
rule overloaded: person t is overloaded if t.load > 24
? person t is overloaded

? person s clashes_on slot k
? person t load number n and t is lecturer
